# What's new

Release notes for the people using this host, kept by its administrator.
Copy to /etc/gah/whats-new.md (root-owned, 0644) to switch them on.

Each `## ` section is one announcement, newest first. At startup a person is
shown the sections they have not seen yet; someone who has never seen any is
shown only the newest. Seen is recorded when they send their first prompt.
/whats-new shows every section. Anything above the first `## ` is ignored.

Write for the person at the keyboard, not for whoever maintains gah: what
changed for them and what, if anything, they should do differently. Keep a
section to a few lines; the startup view shows the first dozen. The heading is
the section's identity, so give each one a date and do not reuse a heading.

## 2026-01-15 — new default model

- New sessions now start on Model B, which is faster on long tickets.
- Model A is still available: /model to switch.
